1. Agreement
This agreement governs your use of the iSelfie SDK, including its binaries, resources,
documentation and sample code (the "SDK"). By downloading, integrating or using the SDK, you
accept this agreement on behalf of yourself or the organization you represent ("you"). If your
organization has a separate signed agreement with AiZtech Labs Inc. ("AiZtech") that covers the
SDK, that agreement prevails where the two conflict.

2. Account and credentials
The SDK works only with an iSelfie organization account and the plan of that account, including
free trials. Your use of the SDK is subject to that plan's limits and fees and to the terms that
apply to your account. You must keep your API key and other account credentials confidential:
the API key belongs on your servers only and must never be included in an application. When your
plan or free trial ends, or its usage limits are reached, the SDK stops performing scans until the
plan is renewed.

3. License grant
While your account has an active plan or free trial, AiZtech grants you a limited, non-exclusive,
non-transferable, non-sublicensable and revocable license to:
  (a) integrate the SDK into your applications that use the iSelfie services;
  (b) distribute the SDK, in object-code form only, as part of those applications to their end
      users; and
  (c) use, copy and modify the sample code and code snippets in the SDK's documentation, solely
      to integrate the SDK into those applications.

4. Restrictions
Except as allowed in Section 3(c), you may not:
  (a) distribute, sell, lease or sublicense the SDK on its own, or as part of another SDK,
      library or development tool;
  (b) modify the SDK or create derivative works of it;
  (c) decompile, disassemble or reverse engineer the SDK, or attempt to extract its source code,
      models, algorithms or validation logic, except to the extent that applicable law expressly
      permits it despite this restriction;
  (d) circumvent or interfere with the SDK's authentication, plan checks, usage limits or
      security;
  (e) use the SDK or its outputs to build or improve a competing product or service;
  (f) remove or alter any proprietary notice in the SDK; or
  (g) use the SDK in violation of any applicable law or regulation.

5. Data and privacy
AiZtech processes raw signals and test results to provide, operate, maintain, secure, and improve
the iSelfie services in accordance with its Privacy Policy and applicable data protection laws.
Any secondary use of personal or health-related data, including training or improving AI models
where additional consent is required, will be subject to such consent.

6. Your applications and end users
You are responsible for your applications and for your relationship with their end users,
including your terms of use, privacy notices, any consent required by law to collect and share
health information, and app-store disclosures. The SDK's outputs are general wellness
information. The SDK is not a medical device and does not provide medical advice, diagnosis or
treatment; you may not present your application or the SDK's outputs as such without AiZtech's
prior written consent and any regulatory approval required.

